    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. Your music and your data</h2>
      <p>Orbit plays music you already have. We do not sell, license or host music, and we do not provide a catalogue. You are responsible for having the rights to the files in your library and for complying with the law where you live.</p>
      <p>Your files, library database, ratings, tags, playlists and play history live on your Server and your devices. You are responsible for backing up and securing your Server. How we handle the little data that does reach us is described in our <a href="{{ '/apps/orbit/privacy/' | url }}">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. Orbit Pro subscription</h2>
      <p>Orbit Pro is an auto-renewable subscription sold through the App&nbsp;Store, billed monthly or yearly. The current price is shown in the App in your local currency before you subscribe.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Payment is charged to your Apple Account when you confirm the purchase. Apple handles billing, receipts, refunds and payment details; we never see your payment information.</li>
        <li>The subscription renews automatically for the same period unless you cancel at least 24 hours before the end of the current period. You can manage or cancel it in your Apple Account settings at any time; cancelling stops renewal but keeps Orbit Pro active until the end of the period already paid.</li>
        <li>When we offer a free trial, it converts to a paid subscription at the end of the trial unless you cancel before then. Any unused portion of a free trial is forfeited when you purchase a subscription.</li>
        <li>One subscription covers the Apps on every supported Apple device signed in to the same Apple Account, and can be shared with your family through Family Sharing.</li>
        <li>Refund requests are handled by Apple under the App&nbsp;Store terms.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The features included in Orbit Pro are listed in the App. We may add, change or retire Pro features over time; we will not remove a feature you paid for during the period you paid for it without offering a remedy.</p>
      <p>The free tier of Orbit, including full-quality playback of your library at home, does not require a subscription.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. Orbit Cloud</h2>
      <p>Orbit Cloud is provided as part of Orbit Pro and stops working when your subscription ends; your library and everything on your Server are unaffected.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>The relay carries audio and data between your devices and your Server, encrypted end to end. We cannot read what passes through it.</li>
        <li>Backups made through Orbit Cloud are encrypted on your Server with a passphrase only you hold. We cannot decrypt them and cannot recover them if you lose the passphrase.</li>
        <li>Relay traffic is subject to fair use. We may limit or throttle accounts whose usage is far outside normal personal listening, and will tell you if we do.</li>
        <li>Orbit Cloud is offered as is, without an uptime guarantee. We may change or discontinue parts of it with reasonable notice.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

